@startuml hotel-0c-asset-pipeline
title Hotel-0c asset pipeline

package "assets/Hotel/ (gitignored, local-only)" {
  folder "raw-heic/**" as RawHeic
  folder "raw-png/**" as RawPng
  folder "png/** (hand-curated)" as CuratedPng
  file "full-board.glb\n(combined Blender scene,\nuser-authored, ~109MB)" as RawGlb
}

package "public/assets/hotel/ (versioned, served)" {
  folder "dice/" as PubDice
  folder "perm-dice/" as PubPermDice
  folder "property-cards/" as PubCards
  folder "gardens/" as PubGardens
  folder "banknotes/" as PubBanknotes
  file "full-board.glb\n(compressed, ~11MB)" as PubGlb
}

RawHeic --> RawPng : scripts/convert-hotel-heic.mjs\n(mechanical mirror, no curation)
RawHeic --> CuratedPng : hand-picked/renamed earlier\n(Hotel-0a board reading round)

CuratedPng --> PubDice : manual copy (implementation-time)
CuratedPng --> PubPermDice : manual copy
CuratedPng --> PubCards : manual copy
CuratedPng --> PubGardens : manual copy
CuratedPng --> PubBanknotes : manual copy

RawGlb --> PubGlb : scripts/compress-hotel-glb.mjs\n(@gltf-transform/cli: resize→jpeg→dedup,\nNOT optimize — that flattens/joins nodes,\nbreaking name-based lookup)

note right of RawGlb
  Hotel-0c.2 — one combined, hand-positioned
  Blender scene: 8 hotels × building tiers
  (<Hotel>-<tier>, or bare <Hotel> for the
  single-tier Boomerang), <Hotel>-garden,
  stairs-<space>-<lotId> per possible
  staircase space, car-<space> per track
  space + car-0-<color> per parking slot,
  board/Bank/cityHall. Every object carries
  its own baked position/rotation/scale —
  read directly, no more eyeballed anchors.
end note

package "src/client" {
  component "useGLTFScene\n(cached GLTFLoader,\nrenderer-agnostic)" as UseGLTFScene
  component "GLTFSceneObject\n(single named object,\nscale is optional/additive)" as GLTFSceneObject
  component "ScannedModel\n(.obj+.mtl, renderer-agnostic,\nunused by Hotel now — kept for\nfuture phone-scanned models)" as ScannedModel
  component "HotelModelObject\n(Hotel-specific: position+scale\nused AS-IS, wrapped in a single\nHOTEL_UP_ROTATION group)" as HotelModelObject
  component "useHotelSpacePositions\n(reads car-N baked positions,\nX/Z as-is, Y/Z sign-flipped to\nmatch HOTEL_UP_ROTATION)" as UseHotelSpacePositions
  component "LoopTrackBoard3D /\ncomputeLoopPositions\n(sceneScale prop, default 1)" as LoopTrack
  component "HotelGamePage\n(HotelBoardModel, HotelBuildingClusters,\nHotelCarToken)" as HotelGamePage
  component "HotelModelViewerPage\n(/games/hotel/model-viewer —\nraw, uncorrected .glb inspector,\nclick-to-see name/transform)" as HotelModelViewerPage
  component "OwnedLotsPanel + Modal\n(cards, decorative)" as OwnedLotsPanel
  component "AnimatedDie" as AnimatedDie
}

PubGlb ..> UseGLTFScene : url (cached once,\nshared by every\nnamed-object lookup)
UseGLTFScene <.. GLTFSceneObject
UseGLTFScene <.. HotelModelObject
UseGLTFScene <.. UseHotelSpacePositions
UseGLTFScene <.. HotelModelViewerPage : same cached scene,\nrendered with ZERO correction

PubDice ..> AnimatedDie : face textures
PubPermDice ..> AnimatedDie
PubCards ..> OwnedLotsPanel
PubGardens ..> OwnedLotsPanel
PubBanknotes ..> OwnedLotsPanel

HotelModelObject <.. HotelGamePage : HotelBoardModel (board/Bank/cityHall)\nHotelBuildingClusters (tiers/garden/stairs)\nHotelCarToken (car-1 shape, tinted per player)
UseHotelSpacePositions <.. HotelGamePage : positions prop\n(falls back to computeSplineLoopPositions\nuntil the model loads)
LoopTrack <.. HotelGamePage : custom S-shaped\ncontrol points (fallback only)
AnimatedDie <.. HotelGamePage : move / permit roll display

note bottom of HotelModelObject
  The whole raw scene loads with "up"
  pointing at world -Y — confirmed
  directly by the USER, via
  HotelModelViewerPage, after THREE
  earlier rounds of per-object rotation
  math each looked right in isolated
  testing and were each wrong once
  checked against a harder live case
  (decompose-and-recover-Ry(θ); reset to
  identity; a Ry(θ)+180° "fix" that still
  didn't hold up under renewed testing).

  Round 4: the user asked to step back
  and see the RAW, uncorrected file
  directly (HotelModelViewerPage was
  built for exactly this), then reported
  precisely: "up is -Y, mirror it to
  +Y". A literal single-axis mirror
  (scale -1 on Y) was tried first and
  immediately broke every piece of board
  text (rendered backwards) — a true
  reflection always reverses
  handedness/readability, which "just
  upside down" didn't actually call for.

  The real, final fix: a single GLOBAL
  180° ROTATION around X
  (HOTEL_UP_ROTATION, hotelModelAssets.ts)
  wrapping only real model content (never
  the fallback placeholders, which are
  already correct). A rotation flips Y
  the same way a mirror would, but
  preserves handedness, so text stays
  readable. Verified against all three
  ground truths at once: readable board
  text, buildings (Boomerang, Royal-1)
  standing upright, and the drawn "Start"
  arrow lined up with the real car/token
  positions. See
  hotel-0c-specifikacio.md §5.8.
end note

@enduml
